      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{58c6a39d9a1fa64abf0edc9e|full_name}: Looks like \"pomo\" trips the filter and turns into \"corno\"  since \"m\" might be used as a replacement for \"rn\" in \"porno\". Interestingly, deleting \"anthropomorphism\" from your description also causes the other words that got mangled (like won -> vvon) to display correctly. Completely agree that they should consider including an error message saying something is wrong instead of mangling the string and even if they don't, probably should look into why parts of the string that don't contain filtered words are getting affected.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
